WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.868
Welcome to Frog Bot. In the next few minutes you will see how to work with your own team of AI agents, right on your computer.

00:00:09.268 --> 00:00:20.931
The first time you open Frog Bot, paste a Claude or OpenAI API key and click Start. Your browser then asks you to allow the ROS dashboard, once.

00:00:21.331 --> 00:00:29.369
Frog is your lead agent. Just tell it what you need, in plain words, like you would tell a coworker.

00:00:29.769 --> 00:00:38.917
To add a teammate, press the plus button and choose New agent. Give it a name, pick an emoji, and describe its job.

00:00:39.317 --> 00:00:53.264
Put agents in a group, and they work together in front of you. Type at, and a name, to talk to one of them. When two agents work together, you see them glow, with a beam between them.

00:00:53.664 --> 00:01:11.996
Under the message box you choose a mode. Ask first, asks before changing things. Auto, just gets it done. Plan, only makes a plan, and gives you a Run this plan button. Click the mode, or press Shift and Tab to switch.

00:01:12.396 --> 00:01:21.195
Anything that sends a message, posts, or deletes, always asks you first. You choose Allow, or Don't allow.

00:01:21.595 --> 00:01:29.728
If an agent needs you in a different chat, a bar appears at the top of whatever you are looking at, with the buttons right there.

00:01:30.128 --> 00:01:42.430
Open Integrations, at the bottom left, to see your connected apps. The ROS dashboard and the browser are built in, and you can add Slack, Notion, GitHub, and more.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:52.128
The Logs tab shows everything that happened, with the date and time. And in Settings, Save tokens keeps your AI costs low.

00:01:52.528 --> 00:02:02.241
That is all you need. Give your team its first job. Frog Bot keeps working from the tray, as long as your computer is on.
